      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-24",
        "notes": "Read all five steps and exact spectral, positivity and orthogonal-invariance suppliers. For arbitrary feasible Z, W=U^TZU has nonnegative diagonal. Squared entry distance splits into diagonal scalar minima and nonnegative off-diagonal squares. Each scalar minimum is unique including lambda=0, and simultaneous equality forces W=diag(lambda+). This proves existence, uniqueness and basis independence for repeated/negative/zero eigenvalues, including d=1 and A=0. Finite decomposition needs no AC. Higham Theorem 2.1 pp.105-106 and Bindel section 6 PDF p.5 checked; their solution agrees with the locally proved formula. Reader locator correction accepted; no unresolved defect."
      }
