      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-24",
        "notes": "Read all three steps and exact F1-F4 suppliers. Outside the cone a negative quadratic witness is nonzero, so rho=-v^TAv/(2||v||²)>0. Entry Cauchy-Schwarz and ||vv^T||F=||v||² keep the whole rho-ball negative. Complement-ball criterion proves closedness. d=1 and singular/zero cone boundary are included; d=0 is excluded. One existential witness uses no AC. Reader explicitly supplies the norm-induced metric and the exact norm-axiom theorem; accepted. Bindel section 6 PDF p.5 and Higham Theorem 2.1 pp.105-106 checked. No unresolved proof defect."
