      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-24",
        "notes": "Checked all four steps and exact F1-F5 supplier statements. Real symmetric PSD form gives a nonnegative self-adjoint operator; the S* S characterization produces a square real L with M=L^TL. Entry expansion and unique nonnegative roots yield distance=||L(x-xprime)||2. Norm sign symmetry, zero diagonal and triangle then apply to every triple. M=0 and singular M are allowed; separation is expressly not asserted and squared distance is not claimed to satisfy triangle. d>=1; finite existential factorization uses no AC. Reader only corrected Bellet printed pp.9-10; current proof unchanged and sound."
