      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-24",
        "notes": "Checked all four steps against the complete isometry supplier and exact convexity, subgradient, metric-topology and ball definitions. Linear bijection preserves convex combinations; its surjectivity is essential in mapping an arbitrary outside Euclidean point back to a complement ball, hence image closedness follows (not a generic continuous-image claim). Inner-product preservation transports the global supporting inequality for all image-domain points. G is a symmetric-space subgradient, as required for svec. Empty C makes the first conclusions vacuous and the conditional M,G premise impossible; singleton/full C and t=0,1 are valid. No existence of subgradients is asserted and no AC is used. No defect."
