        "notes": "Read all four steps and exact objective, trace, finite-sum and convexity definitions. Entry expansion makes each q linear for symmetric M, including indefinite M in the extended objective. Positive part of an affine function satisfies convexity directly by bounding zero and the affine combination. Nonnegative weights mu and 1-mu preserve it, including endpoints and empty target/impostor sets. Quadratic-form inequalities prove convexity of the PSD cone without positivity of eigenvalues or an existence claim for a minimizer. Fixed targets are essential and retained. Weinberger-Saul section 3.4 pp.220-221 agrees with the matrix formulation. No defect, AC use or diagram obligation."
