            "F5",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "If $h_{ijl}(M)>0$, then $\\phi(M)=h_{ijl}(M)$ and $\\phi(N)\\ge h_{ijl}(N)=\\phi(M)+\\langle D_{ijl},N-M\\rangle_F$ for every $N$. If $h_{ijl}(M)\\le0$, then $\\phi(M)=0$ and $\\phi(N)\\ge0=\\phi(M)+\\langle0,N-M\\rangle_F$ for every $N$. Hence $\\gamma_{ijl}(M)D_{ijl}$ is a subgradient of this hinge, including the selected zero coefficient at equality.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
