        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "Each $C_{ij}$ and $D_{ijl}$ is symmetric, so their weighted sum $G(M)$ is symmetric. Each pull term is linear with Frobenius subgradient $C_{ij}$. Adding its supporting equality to the hinge supporting inequalities in step 2.1, weighted by the nonnegative coefficients $1-\\mu$ and $\\mu$, proves $F_\\mu(N)\\ge F_\\mu(M)+\\langle G(M),N-M\\rangle_F$ for every $N\\in\\mathbb S_+^d$. Thus $G(M)$ is a subgradient by [F3].",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
