      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-24",
        "notes": "Read all four steps, all nine facts and exact current generic algorithm/best-average theorem, projection theorem, completeness/Hilbert/AComega definitions and local suppliers. Dimension m=d(d+1)/2>=1 meets the Euclidean completeness and generic algorithm domains. Zero matrix makes the cone nonempty; closedness, convexity and isometry supply a closed convex coordinate domain. Inner-product transport gives valid oracle vectors with norm<=Bdata. Spectral clipping is the unique projection, so the matrix execution is the generic run. Assumed attained Mstar maps bijectively to a minimizer, and isometry gives initial distance R. Positive steps and T>=1 ensure AT>0, a finite least-index best point and feasible weighted average. Applied supplier estimate uses iterates 0 through T-1, not MT. R=0, Bdata=0, empty target/impostor sets, mu endpoints, singular matrices and repeated eigenvalues introduce no division by zero. AComega is explicitly assumed only for the abstract Hilbert projection route selecting a minimizing sequence; no full AC is used or necessity claimed. Bubeck section 3.1 and Bertsekas Lecture15 provide context, while the local generic supplier proves the exact variable-step finite bound without compactness. No defect."
