      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-24",
        "notes": "Read all three verification steps and actual objective, explicit subgradient and finite LMNN algorithm. With d=1,n=2, one label, opposite singleton target sets and mu=0, both pull matrices are [1], no impostors exist, F([m])=2m for m>=0 and optimum is m=0. Starting m=2, G=2 and eta=1/4 give positive preprojection m=3/2, so clipping leaves it unchanged. Objective 4 to 3 is strictly decreasing but gap 3 persists. T=1 is admissible; this is a statement about the returned final point, not the generic best-observed point (which is M0 for this budget). No asymptotic failure or generalization claim is made, and no AC is used by explicit scalar clipping. No defect."
